# Deploy @@APP_NAME@@ in the AI Trust Platform — UI guide

GENERATED by `marketplace/tools/prepare-app`. A copy-paste checklist to add **@@APP_NAME@@** to the
Marketplace **through the UI**, yourself. Every field value is filled in for this app.

> The deployable image is **`ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:sso`** (the sidecar-wrapped app), built and published to
> GitHub Container Registry by `.github/workflows/publish-image.yml` on push to `@@BRANCH@@`. The GHCR
> package is private by default → deploy it as a private-registry image (a GitHub token at Deploy time),
> or make the package public to skip the token.

## Before you start

- Sign in to the platform as a **Platform Administrator** (`marketplace:manage`) — that's who sees the
  **Marketplace** nav item.
- Know your platform's **internal** Keycloak issuer (container-reachable), e.g.
  `http://keycloak:8080/realms/ai-trust`.
- Have a **GitHub PAT with `read:packages`** ready to pull the private image. *(Skip if the package is public.)*
- Confirm the image is published: the repo's **Actions** tab shows a green `publish-image` run and the
  package exists under **Packages**.

## Step 1 — Add the service

Marketplace → **“Add a service (internal — deployed on this cluster)”**:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Display name** | `@@APP_NAME@@` |
| **Slug (URL-safe)** | `@@SLUG@@` |
| **Type** (radio cards) | **Server app — prebuilt image** |
| **Image reference** | `ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:sso` |
| **App port** | `@@LISTEN_PORT@@` |
| **Platform SSO** | ✅ tick |
| **Open in a new tab** | ⬜ leave unticked (embedded) |
| **Private registry** | ✅ tick *(untick only if the package is public)* |
| **Environment variables (optional)** | `OIDC_ISSUER_INTERNAL=http://keycloak:8080/realms/ai-trust` |

Click **Add to catalog**. A card appears with badges `pending`, `server app`, `private image`,
`SSO · role-gated`.

> **App port must be `@@LISTEN_PORT@@`** — that's the sidecar's port, which the platform proxies to. The
> app itself runs internally on `@@UPSTREAM_PORT@@`.

## Step 2 — Deploy

Click **Deploy**. With **Private registry** ticked, the first click reveals **Registry username** (your
GitHub username) and **Registry token / password** (a `read:packages` PAT — *“used only to pull the
image — never stored”*). Fill both, click **Deploy** again → status `running`.

## Step 3 — Enable it for a role

When `running`, use **Enable for role…** → pick a role (e.g. **Platform Administrator**) → **Apply**.
The app is hidden from non-operators until a role is enabled.

## Step 4 — Use it

The app appears in the sidebar under **Services** for users in the enabled role. Click it → it opens
embedded → you're logged in via the **platform** (the sidecar). Then @@APP_NAME@@ is served through the
sidecar. *(If @@APP_NAME@@ has its own login, you'll see it after the platform login.)*

## Check what you configured

Click **Configuration** on the card:
```
Kind          image
Image ref     ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:sso
App port      @@LISTEN_PORT@@
Open mode     same window (embedded)
Platform SSO  on (role-gated)
Environment   OIDC_ISSUER_INTERNAL = http://keycloak:8080/realms/ai-trust
```

## Confirm it worked (optional, terminal)

The container is `mkt-@@SLUG@@`.
```bash
docker exec mkt-@@SLUG@@ env | grep -E 'OIDC_|^ISSUER='
docker exec ai-trust-platform-git-shell-1 \
  wget -S -qO- "http://mkt-@@SLUG@@:@@LISTEN_PORT@@/login" 2>&1 | grep -i location
# → Location: <keycloak>/realms/ai-trust/protocol/openid-connect/auth?client_id=aitrust-app-@@SLUG@@&...
```

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| Login 500 / `ECONNREFUSED` | wrong/missing `OIDC_ISSUER_INTERNAL` | point it at the in-cluster Keycloak |
| Tile not in sidebar | not enabled for your role, or not `running` | Step 3; confirm `running` |
| Deploy 401/403 "not pullable" | bad/missing GitHub token or package not published | green Actions run + `read:packages` PAT + correct ref |
| App loads but assets 404 | app hardcodes root-absolute URLs | set `PUBLIC_PATHS` or a base-href (see sidecar README) |

Full background: `marketplace/docs/onboard-an-app.md`.
